00:47:05,000 --> 00:47:11,000
Superbad is a 2007 American coming-of-age teen buddy comedy film directed by Greg
Mottola, written by Seth Rogen and Evan Goldberg, and produced by Judd Apatow.

11
00:51:47,500 --> 00:51:53,500
It stars Jonah Hill and Michael Cera as Seth and Evan, two
teenagers about to graduate from high school.

12
00:56:30,000 --> 00:56:36,000
Before graduating, the boys want to party and lose their
virginity, but their plan proves harder than expected.

13
01:01:12,500 --> 01:01:18,500
Christopher Mintz-Plasse (in his film debut), Rogen, Bill Hader, Martha
MacIsaac, and Emma Stone (in her film debut) provide supporting roles.

14
01:05:55,000 --> 01:06:01,000
Rogen and Goldberg wrote the script during their teenage years.

15
01:10:37,500 --> 01:10:43,500
It is loosely based on their experience in Grade 12 at Point Grey
Secondary School in Vancouver during the 1990s.

16
01:15:20,000 --> 01:15:26,000
The main characters have the same given names as the two writers.

17
01:20:02,500 --> 01:20:08,500
Rogen was also initially intended to play Seth, but due to age and physical size this was changed, and Hill went on to portray Seth,
while Rogen portrayed the irresponsible Officer Michaels, opposite Saturday Night Live star Hader as Officer Slater.

18
01:24:45,000 --> 01:24:51,000
Superbad premiered at Grauman's Chinese Theatre on August 13, 2007, and was
theatrically released in the United States four days later on August 17, 2007.

19
01:29:27,500 --> 01:29:33,500
The film received positive reviews, with critics praising the dialogue and the chemistry
between the two leads as well as the performances of the supporting cast.

20
01:34:10,000 --> 01:34:16,000
The film also proved financially successful, grossing
$170.8 million on a $17.5–20 million budget.

21
01:38:52,500 --> 01:38:58,500
The film has since become a cult classic, considered
among the best comedy films of all time.

22
01:43:35,000 --> 01:43:41,000
The film explores themes of high school, police, alcohol, chaos, nerd.

23
01:48:17,500 --> 01:48:23,500
The tone is lighthearted.
